# No useless scrollbars

Do not put `overflow: auto`, `overflow-y: auto`, or `overflow: scroll` on a layout “just in case”.

If there is empty space on the page, the content must **fit**. Shrink padding, gaps, card `min-height`, chart height, or use two columns. Do not open a scrollport.

A Windows scrollbar (white track, arrows) on a dark hub with empty background beside it is always a bug.

## Do

- Default: `overflow: hidden` on full-height shells (`100dvh` hubs, shells, splits).
- Scroll **one** pane only when that pane’s content is truly taller than the pane (long essay, long passage).
- If cards almost fit, cut `min-height` / padding until they fit. Do not add a scroller for 20px.

## Do not

```css
/* BAD — inner scroll while the viewport still has empty space */
.pr-hub__tasks { flex: 1; min-height: 0; overflow: auto; }
.pw-model-page { overflow: auto; padding-bottom: 20px; }

/* BAD — scrollbar always reserved */
overflow-y: scroll;
scrollbar-gutter: stable;
```

```css
/* GOOD — catalog / folder / chart page that should fit */
.pr-hub { height: 100dvh; overflow: hidden; }
.pr-hub__tasks { overflow: hidden; }
```

Never nest two scrollbars. Never add a scrollbar around a chart.
